{"created": "2026-04-15T14:26:49.632160+00:00", "modified": "2026-04-16T08:49:19.743285+00:00", "id": 19367714, "conceptrecid": "19367713", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19367714", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.19367713", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19367714", "metadata": {"title": "CAVERS: Multimodal SLAM Data from a Natural Karstic Cave with Ground Truth Motion Capture", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19367714", "publication_date": "2026-04-01", "description": "<p></p>\n<p>CAVERS is a multimodal dataset collected at Cueva de la Victoria in M&aacute;laga, Spain, comprising sequences from an RGB-D camera, an IMU, a rotating 3D LiDAR, and a near-IR thermal camera. Sequences are recorded under two independent conditions: illumination, either in full darkness or using an LED light source mounted on the sensor rig, and platform, with the sensor rig operated either handheld or installed on a wheeled rover. Accurate and high frequency rig&rsquo;s pose and velocity ground truth are provided for localization-targeted sequences, as provided by an Optitrack motion capture system installed in the cave.&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Franchini, Giacomo", "affiliation": "Politecnico di Torino", "orcid": "0009-0009-5641-8346"}, {"name": "Rodr\u00edguez-Mart\u00ednez, David", "affiliation": "Universidad de M\u00e1laga", "orcid": "0000-0003-4817-9225"}, {"name": "Alfonso Mart\u00ednez Petersen", "affiliation": "Universidad de M\u00e1laga"}, {"name": "P\u00e9rez del Pulgar Mancebo, Carlos Jes\u00fas", "affiliation": "Universidad de M\u00e1laga", "orcid": "0000-0001-5819-8310"}, {"name": "Chiaberge, Marcello", "affiliation": "Politecnico di Torino Dipartimento di Elettronica e Telecomunicazioni", "orcid": "0000-0002-1921-0126"}], "keywords": ["Underground robotics", "Caves", "SLAM"], "dates": [{"type": "created"}], "version": "0.0.1", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentS